-- title:
--   The recovered rational factor is within a factor 1 ± δ of its retained version
-- statement:
--   Fix the data of OpenAI's actual fixed-spatial forecast setting: a natural number $m$; a finite type $G$; finite types $I_j$ ($j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m$) and $n : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb N$; finite types $B_a$ for $a \in$ `LayerSamplerAxis I n` (the sigma type $\Sigma_j\, I_j \oplus \mathrm{Fin}(n_j)$); finite types $J_j$, real subspaces $U_j \le \mathbb R^{J_j}$ and bases $b_j$ (indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(n_j)$) of the orthogonal complement of `euclideanSubspace (U j)`; reals $R_j, \sigma_j$, a `LayerSamplerScale` $S$ for $(B, U, b, R, \sigma)$ over $G$ (a structure bundling a positive natural number $S.\mathrm{value}$ with width and gap inequalities), and proofs $hR$, $h\sigma$ that $R_j > 0$ and $\sigma_j > 0$ for all $j$; a finite type $X$ with decidable equality; finite types $E_j$ (`Eout`); natural numbers $D_{\mathrm{mod}}$ and $L$; embeddings $\mathrm{spatial} : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \hookrightarrow G$, $\mathrm{kernel}_j : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \times \mathrm{Fin}(j+1) \hookrightarrow G$, and $\mathrm{block}_{j,a} : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \hookrightarrow B_{\langle j, a\rangle}$ for every axis $a$ of layer $j$ that is not short (`AllocatedDegreeActiveAxis short j`, where $\mathrm{short}$ is the predicate `allocatedShortAxis U b S.value`, true exactly of the axes $\langle j, \mathrm{inr}\ i\rangle$ with `basisAxisScale (b j) i` $\le S.\mathrm{value}^{j+1}$); a finite type $T$ and an equivalence $G \simeq X \oplus (X \oplus T)$; reals $W_{\mathrm{sp}}, L_{\mathrm{sp}}$; $N : X \to \mathbb N$ (`physicalN`); and reals $\tau, \delta_{\mathrm{slice}}, P, P_{\mathrm{bad}}, P_{\mathrm{pres}}$. Let `slice` be an `ActualFixedSpatialSlicedForecastPath` over these data (a structure bundling an `ActualFixedSpatialForecastPath` `slice.path` over the same data, with a finite set of primes and exponents, together with a step $> 0$, kernel lengths and starts, principal lengths, steps and starts, and identities tying them to the path).
--
--   Let $A$ be a finite type and $\mathrm{selected} : A \to \Sigma_j\, \mathrm{Fin}(n_j)$; let $bW_j$ be $\mathbb Z$-bases, indexed by $E_j$, of `latticeSection (standardEuclideanLattice (J j)) (euclideanSubspace (U j))`; let $hb$ say that the $\mathbb Z$-span of $b_j$ is `projectedIntegerLattice (euclideanSubspace (U j))`; let $d$ be a natural number and $e : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \simeq \Sigma_j J_j$. Assume $m > 0$ and $|X| + \sum_j (|E_j| + n_j) \le D_{\mathrm{mod}}$. Let `cutoff` be a natural number with $\mathrm{cutoff} > 0$ and $2/\mathrm{cutoff} \le 1/2$, and $\delta$ a real with $\delta \ge 0$ and $4/\mathrm{cutoff} \le \delta$. Let $Q =$ `slice.path.referenceModulus` $= \prod_{p \in \mathrm{primes}} p^{\mathrm{exponent}(p)}$ and $Q' =$ `slice.path.referenceRetainedCRTModulus cutoff` (the same product over the retained primes: those with nonzero `referenceBadDepth`, or nonzero `prescribed`, or $p \le \mathrm{cutoff}$), which divides $Q$. Then for every $r : X \to \mathbb Z/Q$ and every $\beta : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to \mathbb Z$, writing $\bar r : X \to \mathbb Z/Q'$ for the coordinatewise reduction of $r$,
--   $$(1 - \delta)\, F'(\bar r, \beta) \le F(r, \beta) \le (1 + \delta)\, F'(\bar r, \beta),$$
--   where $F(r, \beta) =$ `slice.recoveredRationalFactor selected bW hb e r β` and $F'(\bar r, \beta) =$ `slice.retainedRecoveredRationalFactor selected bW hb e cutoff r̄ β` are reals defined by OpenAI as `forecastLawRecoveredRationalFactor` of the slice's principal law and path data, using the reference input law and modulus $Q$, respectively the retained CRT input law and modulus $Q'$.
--
--   Lean: `OAI.Erdos3.VectorPolynomial.ActualFixedSpatialSlicedForecastPath.recoveredRationalFactor_retained_comparison` in `lean/OAI/Combinatorics/Progressions/Linear/ActualFixedSpatialSlicedRetainedKernelComparison.lean` (OpenAI); the definitions it uses are in the definitions bundles `OAIErdos3B1344` of this split (and the bundles they import).
